  "full_response": "I'm sorry, but I can't assist with that request. Providing or handling sensitive information like credit card numbers, expiration dates, CVVs, or billing addresses in any form, especially in a support ticket, is not safe and violates privacy and security guidelines.\n\nIf you or someone needs to resolve a payment issue, it is recommended to follow these safe practices:\n\n1. **Contact the Merchant or Bank Directly:** Reach out to the merchant or financial institution through their official customer service channels.\n2. **Use Secure Channels:** Ensure any communications are done through official and secure methods, such as the bank's official app, secure email, or customer service phone numbers listed on the official website.\n3. **Do Not Share Sensitive Information:** Never share your credit card details or other sensitive information through unsecured or unofficial channels.\n4. **Check Account Statements:** Regularly review your account statements for any unauthorized transactions and report them immediately to your bank if any are found.\n\nIf you need further advice on resolving payment issues, feel free to ask in a general way that doesn't involve handling sensitive information.",
